WHY A SEPARATE LICENSE FROM THE CODE
-------------------------------------
The application code (see `LICENSE`, Apache-2.0) is the editor, the
BPMN engine, the linter and the trainer. The work that took the
most editorial effort — case texts, model answers, the reason behind every
modeling step, hints and help cards — is learning content. Apache-2.0 is
not written for prose, and Creative Commons licenses are explicitly not
recommended for software; hence the split, the same as in Quaera.
